# Compose UI — reuse before inventing

When adding or extending screens, **compose** from existing primitives and shared widgets. Do not rebuild the same card, pill, or chrome in a second screen.

Folder roles: [screen-component-layers.mdc](screen-component-layers.mdc).

## Before writing markup

1. **Host screen first.** List sibling rows/cards on the screen that will show the control. Match **that** family.
2. Check **`src/ui-components/`** for a primitive.
3. Search **`src/components/<feature>/`** for an existing widget for this control.
4. If the same control is (or will be) on **two or more screens**, extract a shared widget **before** copying.

## Planned shared widgets

- **`WhiskeyCard`** — one card for both the Search result list and the Scan Bottle candidates.
- **`Pill`** — one outlined pill for category, similarity percentage, and “Best guess”.

Two screens, one component, two thin hosts.

## Where it lives

| Kind | Put it in |
| --- | --- |
| Generic look (no feature copy, no data) | `@/ui-components/*` |
| Feature-specific but reused | `@/components/<feature>/`, composed from ui-components |
| One-screen chrome | The view — still use primitives |

Do **not** put scan/catalog copy or data access in `ui-components/`.

## Tests

- Behavior (labels, a11y, disabled states) lives on the **shared widget**.
- Screen tests only prove **wiring** (widget mounted, callback/testID, screen-specific copy).
- Do not copy the same test matrix onto every host screen — that is how forks drift.

## Agent behavior

- New typography goes through `Text` variants, not ad-hoc font classes.
- Same user control on N screens → **one** component, **N** thin hosts.
